  "details": "I am well aware that you can't have space in Variable names in C#, but if a beginner is using the visual editor they might not know.\nIf you add space to the variable name, it will throw a exception at you.\n---\nParseException: Expected ':', found 'variable' instead. Line: 4\n---\nSo, any variable name should just be either converted to a non space version or replace space with _\n\nEdit: This can be expanded to any special characters really.",
